The fix was straightforward. The original `fetchAll` in `index.js`:

```js
async function fetchAll(fns) {
  return fns.map(fn => fn());
}
```

used `Array.map()` which calls each async function but only collects their unresolved promises — returning `[Promise {1}, Promise {2}]` instead of their values.

The fix wraps the map with `Promise.all()`:

```js
async function fetchAll(fns) {
  return Promise.all(fns.map(fn => fn()));
}
```

